FDWM's own, after upstream's pertag patch
(https://dwm.suckless.org/patches/pertag/): each tag (slots 1 to 9) and the
view of all nine (slot 0, Alt+0) keeps its own nmaster, mfact, layouts and
bar. Rather than the patch's assignments inside each setter, savepertag()
stores the monitor's settings in the current slot after setlayout,
setmfact, resetmfact (FDWM's), incnmaster, togglebar and dragmfact's drag
in resizemouse, which the patch doesn't know about, and restorepertag()
brings a slot back in view and toggleview. pertagslot() picks the slot
from the tags in view with the scratchpads' tags left out, so a view of
all nine is Alt+0's ~SPTAGMASK, not the patch's ~0, a scratchpad never
changes the slot, and a view holding nothing but a scratchpad keeps it
(the patch would index past the arrays). struct NumTags is the
scratchpads patch's already. The man page says so.

